  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt. Chandrawati vs State Of U.P. And Another on 15 July, 2025 Author: Gautam Chowdhary Bench: Gautam Chowdhary High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:114327 Court No. - 70 Case :- Application U/S 528 Bnss No. - 24551 of 2025 Applicant :- Smt. Chandrawati Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Applicant :- Dinesh Kumar Maurya,Ram Raj Prajapati Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Dr. Gautam Chowdhary,J. 1. 2. This application has been filed for quashing of the proceedings of Case No. 2709 of 2004 (State Vs. Chandrawati) under Section 7/16 Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, Police Station Kotwali, District Shahjahanpur pending in the Court of Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Ist, District Shahjahanpur as well as to quash the non-bailable-warrants order dated 27.05.2015 and also the order dated 03.08.2024 by which process under Section 82 Cr.P.C. has been issued. 3.",
    "facts": "2. This application has been filed for quashing of the proceedings of Case No. 2709 of 2004 (State Vs. Chandrawati) under Section 7/16 Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, Police Station Kotwali, District Shahjahanpur pending in the Court of Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Ist, District Shahjahanpur as well as to quash the non-bailable-warrants order dated 27.05.2015 and also the order dated 03.08.2024 by which process under Section 82 Cr.P.C. has been issued. 3.",
    "arguments": "At this stage, the learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant has so far not been arrested in the above case and the police is seeking to arrest the applicant and there may be coercive processes issued against the applicant by the court concerned therefore, some direction may be issued to the court concerned for consideration of the bail prayer of the applicant. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "At this stage, the learned counsel for the applicant submits that the applicant has so far not been arrested in the above case and the police is seeking to arrest the applicant and there may be coercive processes issued against the applicant by the court concerned therefore, some direction may be issued to the court concerned for consideration of the bail prayer of the applicant. 6.",
